<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Logs on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/</link><description>Recent content in Logs on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>1. Introduction to Logs</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/1-introduction/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/1-introduction/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;You’ve now navigated directly from an &lt;strong&gt;APM&lt;/strong&gt; trace into &lt;strong&gt;Logs&lt;/strong&gt; using the &lt;strong&gt;Related Content&lt;/strong&gt; link. &lt;strong&gt;Logs&lt;/strong&gt; is Splunk Observability Cloud’s no-code interface for exploring and analyzing log data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The key advantage, just as with the &lt;strong&gt;RUM&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;APM&lt;/strong&gt; integration, is that you’re viewing your logs in the context of your previous actions. In this case, that context includes the matching time range &lt;strong&gt;(1)&lt;/strong&gt; from the trace and a filter &lt;strong&gt;(2)&lt;/strong&gt; automatically applied to the &lt;code&gt;trace_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>2. Log Filtering</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/2-log-filtering/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/2-log-filtering/</guid><description>&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Filter to Error Logs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The selected trace contains log records with different severity levels. You’ll first group them by severity, then filter the results to focus on errors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the existing trace ID search filter and time range unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open &lt;strong&gt;Group by (1)&lt;/strong&gt;, search for &lt;em&gt;severity&lt;/em&gt;, and select it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;button class="btn-inline btn-inline--filled" type="button" style="--btn-color: #1d5d99"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Apply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;. The chart now separates the log records by &lt;strong&gt;severity&lt;/strong&gt;, such as &lt;em&gt;info&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;debug&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;error&lt;/strong&gt;. The values shown depend on your selected trace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grouping helps you compare the different &lt;strong&gt;severity&lt;/strong&gt; levels, but it does not remove records from the results. To display only error logs:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>3. Viewing Log Entries</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/3-log-entry/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/splunk4rookies/o11y-rookies-26/modules/1-intro/5-logs/3-log-entry/</guid><description>&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Investigate the Error Message&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have narrowed the results to error logs from the selected trace. Now examine an individual record to find the explanation behind the &lt;strong&gt;payment&lt;/strong&gt; failure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select an error entry in the &lt;strong&gt;Logs table&lt;/strong&gt; to open its details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check the record’s &lt;strong&gt;service&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;hostname&lt;/strong&gt; fields to confirm that it came from the &lt;strong&gt;payment&lt;/strong&gt; service. Other services involved in the trace may also have reported errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read the complete message and examine the associated fields. Scroll through the details if necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs" data-tabs&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs__list" role="tablist"&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-tab-0" class="tabs__btn is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-panel-0" tabindex="0" data-tab-label="Question"&gt;Question&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-tab-1" class="tabs__btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-tab-label="Answer"&gt;Answer&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-panel-0" class="tabs__panel is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-tab-0" data-tab-label="Question"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does the log message reveal about the &lt;em&gt;payment&lt;/em&gt; failure, and what should the development team check to resolve it?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-panel-1" class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-splunk4rookies-o11y-rookies-26-modules-1-intro-5-logs-3-log-entry-md-1-1--0-tab-1" hidden data-tab-label="Answer"&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The message reports that &lt;em&gt;ButtercupPayments&lt;/em&gt; rejected an &lt;em&gt;invalid API token&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The development team should check the payment-provider credentials configured for version &lt;code&gt;v350.10&lt;/code&gt;, correct or replace the invalid token, and verify that payment requests succeed afterward or rollback to &lt;code&gt;v350.9&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/log-observer-log-message.png" alt="Log Message" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>